{"t_ms": 213484, "conversation_id": "v2llm_batch_retrieve_s004", "turn_id": 1, "actor": "system", "event_type": "retrieval_result", "payload": {"passages": ["Visitor Policy\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nVisitors are permitted between 8:00 AM and 10:00 PM after registering at the Front Desk with a valid photo ID. Overnight visitors are not allowed unless officially added to the room reservation and applicable charges have been settled. Hotel management reserves the right to deny entry if security concerns arise.", "# corpus/ \u2014 Hotel Documents\n\n**Owner: Lakshya**\n\n## What this folder is\n\nThe hotel's documents live here: the knowledge the assistant answers from. About 60 short \ndocuments covering things like pool and gym hours, check-in and check-out rules, menus, and \npolicies.\n\n## How to fill it\n\nSee the full instructions in `retrieval/README.md` (Step 1). In short:\n- Write ~60 short documents, one topic per file, as `.txt` or `.md`.\n- Make them realistic and varied.\n- Deliberately plant a few contradictions (e.g. one doc says the pool closes at 10 PM, \n  another says 9 PM) and keep a note of which ones, for a later experiment.\n\nThe index-building script reads every file in this folder, so anything you put here becomes \npart of the searchable knowledge.\n", "Parking Policy\n\nGrand Horizon Hotel & Suites\n\nThe hotel provides complimentary on-site parking for all registered guests throughout their stay. Parking spaces are allocated on a first-come, first-served basis. Dedicated parking is available for guests with disabilities and electric vehicles. The hotel recommends locking vehicles and avoiding leaving valuables inside parked cars"], "scores": [0.6776010990142822, 0.7275017499923706, 0.7597407102584839], "filenames": ["56_visitor_policy.txt", "README.md", "47_parking_v1.txt"], "timing_policy": "sentence_end", "timing_trigger": "sentence_end", "user_end_known_at_finish": true, "launch_offset_ms_vs_user_end": 156, "overlap_with_speech_ms": 0, "forecast_invalidated": false}}
